build: 2026-06-21 v10.34.25 (Patchbay routing goes live — outputs activate on connection)
branch: claude/piano-roll-clip-view-wozlie
includes: The Routing patchbay now actually moves bytes. Making a connection to an output turns it on: connect Music or Body to Art-Net / sACN and the lights run; to ADM-OSC and the immersive object moves; to OSC and the stream goes out; to MIDI Out and your notes reach your DAW. Removing the last connection switches that output back off. (These outputs had no on-screen control in the single-view app before — the patchbay is now their home.) Launch stays lean: no connections means nothing starts, no extra permission prompts; your routes persist. Tap a source, tap a destination — compatible types link directly or via a converter (pitch→colour, bio→MIDI CC), and "Smart patch" wires them all at once. Built on the typed Signal Router and the music→light/spatial adapter. Verified: Xcode Compile Check + CI green.
